<div class="tribe-manual">
	<ManualHeader />

	<ManualPageNav @activePage="cleanup" />

	<div class="container pb-5">

		<div class="alert alert-danger mb-4">
			<strong>This cannot be undone.</strong>
			These steps delete the database, every uploaded file and the deployed
			sites of a Tribe installation. Run the commands from the Tribe folder, the
			one that contains
			<code>docker-compose.yml</code>
			and
			<code>.env</code>.
		</div>

		<div class="steps-container mb-5">

			<div
				class="step-card"
				data-step-name="Back up backup restic mysqldump uploads before deleting"
			>
				<div class="step-header" onclick="toggleStep(this)">
					<span class="step-badge">1</span>
					<span class="step-title">Back Up</span>
					<i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down step-chevron"></i>
				</div>
				<div class="step-body">
					<p>All runtime data lives in two places inside the Tribe folder:</p>
					<ul class="small">
						<li><code>uploads/</code>
							holds the MySQL data, uploaded files, deployed sites, Cronicle,
							Centrifugo, Plausible and Tor data.</li>
						<li><code>.env</code>
							holds the passwords and settings.</li>
					</ul>
					<p class="mb-1">Take a final copy of both if you may need them later.
						With Restic set up, run a last backup:</p>
					<div class="command-block mb-3">
						<button
							class="btn btn-sm copy-btn-block"
							onclick="copyCmd('sudo systemctl start &quot;restic-backup@$(systemd-escape /path/to/tribe).service&quot;', this)"
							type="button"
						>Copy</button>
						<code>sudo systemctl start "restic-backup@$(systemd-escape
							/path/to/tribe).service"</code>
					</div>
					<p class="mb-1">Without Restic, copy the folder while the containers
						are stopped:</p>
					<div class="command-block mb-0">
						<button
							class="btn btn-sm copy-btn-block"
							onclick="copyCmd('docker compose stop && sudo tar -czf ../project-final-backup.tar.gz uploads .env', this)"
							type="button"
						>Copy</button>
						<code>docker compose stop &amp;&amp; sudo tar -czf
							../project-final-backup.tar.gz uploads .env</code>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div
				class="step-card"
				data-step-name="Identify installation PROJECT_NAME docker compose ps containers"
			>
				<div class="step-header" onclick="toggleStep(this)">
					<span class="step-badge">2</span>
					<span class="step-title">Identify the Installation</span>
					<i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down step-chevron"></i>
				</div>
				<div class="step-body">
					<p>Every container, volume and network of an installation is named
						after
						<code>PROJECT_NAME</code>
						in
						<code>.env</code>. Read it first:</p>
					<div class="command-block mb-3">
						<button
							class="btn btn-sm copy-btn-block"
							onclick="copyCmd('grep -E &quot;^(PROJECT_NAME|DB_HOST|DB_NAME|DB_USER)=&quot; .env', this)"
							type="button"
						>Copy</button>
						<code>grep -E "^(PROJECT_NAME|DB_HOST|DB_NAME|DB_USER)=" .env</code>
					</div>
					<p class="mb-1">Then list what belongs to it, replacing
						<code>tribe</code>
						with your
						<code>PROJECT_NAME</code>:</p>
					<div class="command-block mb-3">
						<button
							class="btn btn-sm copy-btn-block"
							onclick="copyCmd('docker ps -a --filter name=tribe_', this)"
							type="button"
						>Copy</button>
						<code>docker ps -a --filter name=project_name_</code>
					</div>
					<div class="alert alert-info mb-0">
						<strong>Which kind of installation is it?</strong>
						A standard installation uses
						<code>docker-compose.yml</code>. A Loom thread also uses
						<code>docker-compose.yml</code>
						and has
						<code>LOOM_PROJECT_NAME</code>
						in its
						<code>.env</code>. A Tor installation also has
						<code>docker-compose.tor.yml</code>
						in its root. The next steps differ for each.
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div
				class="step-card"
				data-step-name="Remove domains nginx vhost uninstall certbot delete certificates"
			>
				<div class="step-header" onclick="toggleStep(this)">
					<span class="step-badge">3</span>
					<span class="step-title">Remove Domains (Nginx)</span>
					<i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down step-chevron"></i>
				</div>
				<div class="step-body">
					<p>Skip this step if you never ran
						<code>node vhost</code>
						for this installation.</p>
					<p class="mb-1">Remove the nginx site file of each domain. The script
						asks for one domain at a time, so run it once for each of Tribe,
						Junction, Dist, Dist PHP and Plausible:</p>
					<div class="command-block mb-3">
						<button
							class="btn btn-sm copy-btn-block"
							onclick="copyCmd('sudo node vhost uninstall', this)"
							type="button"
						>Copy</button>
						<code>sudo node vhost uninstall</code>
					</div>
					<p class="mb-1">The script keeps certificates. Delete each one by
						name:</p>
					<div class="command-block mb-3">
						<button
							class="btn btn-sm copy-btn-block"
							onclick="copyCmd('sudo certbot delete --cert-name junction.domain.tld', this)"
							type="button"
						>Copy</button>
						<code>sudo certbot delete --cert-name junction.domain.tld</code>
					</div>
					<p class="mb-1">Check the remaining nginx configuration and reload it:</p>
					<div class="command-block mb-0">
						<button
							class="btn btn-sm copy-btn-block"
							onclick="copyCmd('sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx', this)"
							type="button"
						>Copy</button>
						<code>sudo nginx -t &amp;&amp; sudo systemctl reload nginx</code>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div
				class="step-card"
				data-step-name="Stop and remove containers docker compose down volumes network thread tor"
			>
				<div class="step-header" onclick="toggleStep(this)">
					<span class="step-badge">4</span>
					<span class="step-title">Remove Containers, Volumes &amp; Network</span>
					<i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down step-chevron"></i>
				</div>
				<div class="step-body">
					<p>This stops every container of the installation and removes the
						containers, the Caddy volumes and the
						<code>PROJECT_NAME_network</code>
						network. Run the command that matches your installation:</p>

					<div class="row g-3">
						<div class="col-md-6">
							<div class="card method-item h-100">
								<div class="card-body">
									<h6><strong>Standard or Loom thread</strong></h6>
									<div class="command-block mb-0">
										<button
											class="btn btn-sm copy-btn-block"
											onclick="copyCmd('docker compose down -v --remove-orphans', this)"
											type="button"
										>Copy</button>
										<code>docker compose down -v --remove-orphans</code>
									</div>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="col-md-6">
							<div class="card method-item h-100">
								<div class="card-body">
									<h6><strong>Tor</strong></h6>
									<div class="command-block mb-0">
										<button
											class="btn btn-sm copy-btn-block"
											onclick="copyCmd('docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.tor.yml down -v --remove-orphans', this)"
											type="button"
										>Copy</button>
										<code>docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f
											docker-compose.tor.yml down -v --remove-orphans</code>
									</div>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="alert alert-warning mt-3 mb-0">
						<strong>Removing a Loom:</strong>
						Threads share the Loom's MySQL and network. Remove every thread of a
						Loom before you remove the Loom itself.
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div
				class="step-card"
				data-step-name="Loom thread drop database user loom_mysql DROP DATABASE DROP USER"
			>
				<div class="step-header" onclick="toggleStep(this)">
					<span class="step-badge">5</span>
					<span class="step-title">Drop the Thread Database (Loom Only)</span>
					<i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down step-chevron"></i>
				</div>
				<div class="step-body">
					<p>Skip this step for a standard or Tor installation. Its database
						lives in
						<code>uploads/mysql</code>
						and is deleted in step 7.</p>
					<p class="mb-1">A thread's database and user live inside the Loom's
						MySQL container, so removing the thread leaves them behind. Drop
						them with the values of
						<code>DB_HOST</code>,
						<code>DB_NAME</code>
						and
						<code>DB_USER</code>
						from the thread's
						<code>.env</code>. You will be asked for the Loom's MySQL root
						password:</p>
					<div class="command-block mb-0">
						<button
							class="btn btn-sm copy-btn-block"
							onclick="copyCmd('docker exec -it db_host mysql -u root -p -e &quot;DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS db_name; DROP USER IF EXISTS \'db_user\'@\'%\';&quot;', this)"
							type="button"
						>Copy</button>
						<code>docker exec -it db_host mysql -u root -p -e "DROP DATABASE
							IF EXISTS db_name; DROP USER IF EXISTS 'db_user'@'%';"</code>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div
				class="step-card"
				data-step-name="Stop backups restic timers systemctl disable snapshots"
			>
				<div class="step-header" onclick="toggleStep(this)">
					<span class="step-badge">6</span>
					<span class="step-title">Stop Backups (Restic)</span>
					<i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down step-chevron"></i>
				</div>
				<div class="step-body">
					<p>Skip this step if this installation was not backed up with Restic.</p>
					<p class="mb-1">Disable the backup and prune timers for the path that
						was backed up, so they stop failing once the folder is gone:</p>
					<div class="command-block mb-3">
						<button
							class="btn btn-sm copy-btn-block"
							onclick="copyCmd('sudo systemctl disable --now &quot;restic-backup@$(systemd-escape /path/to/tribe).timer&quot; &quot;restic-prune@$(systemd-escape /path/to/tribe).timer&quot;', this)"
							type="button"
						>Copy</button>
						<code>sudo systemctl disable --now "restic-backup@$(systemd-escape
							/path/to/tribe).timer" "restic-prune@$(systemd-escape
							/path/to/tribe).timer"</code>
					</div>
					<div class="alert alert-info mb-0">
						<strong>Snapshots stay.</strong>
						Existing snapshots remain in the Restic repository. Delete them
						there only when you are sure you will not need to restore this
						installation.
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div
				class="step-card"
				data-step-name="Delete files folder rm uploads mysql sudo"
			>
				<div class="step-header" onclick="toggleStep(this)">
					<span class="step-badge">7</span>
					<span class="step-title">Delete the Files</span>
					<i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down step-chevron"></i>
				</div>
				<div class="step-body">
					<p>Move out of the Tribe folder and delete it. The command needs
						<code>sudo</code>
						because the containers own the files in
						<code>uploads/mysql</code>
						and other data folders.</p>
					<div class="command-block mb-0">
						<button
							class="btn btn-sm copy-btn-block"
							onclick="copyCmd('cd .. && sudo rm -rf /path/to/tribe', this)"
							type="button"
						>Copy</button>
						<code>cd .. &amp;&amp; sudo rm -rf /path/to/tribe</code>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div
				class="step-card"
				data-step-name="Verify docker ps volume ls network ls leftovers images prune"
			>
				<div class="step-header" onclick="toggleStep(this)">
					<span class="step-badge">8</span>
					<span class="step-title">Verify &amp; Free Disk Space</span>
					<i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down step-chevron"></i>
				</div>
				<div class="step-body">
					<p class="mb-1">Each of these commands should print no rows other than
						the header. Replace
						<code>tribe</code>
						with your
						<code>PROJECT_NAME</code>:</p>
					<div class="command-block mb-3">
						<button
							class="btn btn-sm copy-btn-block"
							onclick="copyCmd('docker ps -a --filter name=tribe_; docker volume ls --filter name=tribe_; docker network ls --filter name=tribe_', this)"
							type="button"
						>Copy</button>
						<code>docker ps -a --filter name=tribe_<br />docker volume ls
							--filter name=tribe_<br />docker network ls --filter name=tribe_</code>
					</div>
					<p class="mb-1">Docker keeps the downloaded images. Remove the images
						that no container uses any more:</p>
					<div class="command-block mb-3">
						<button
							class="btn btn-sm copy-btn-block"
							onclick="copyCmd('docker image prune -a', this)"
							type="button"
						>Copy</button>
						<code>docker image prune -a</code>
					</div>
					<div class="alert alert-warning mb-0">
						<strong>Other projects on the same server:</strong>
						<code>docker image prune -a</code>
						removes every image on the server that no container uses, not only
						Tribe's. Images of existing containers, running or stopped, are
						kept.
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

		</div>

		<ManualFooter />

	</div>
</div>

<ManualScripts />
